# ChoreStrike AI Guidelines

- **Language:** ALL code, comments, commit messages, and documentation must be in **English only**. Chatting with the user in German is allowed.
- **Auto-Commit:** After completing a logical package or bugfix, automatically execute `git add` and `git commit` with a meaningful message. Update docs and backlog accordingly.
- **KISS & DRY:** Keep it simple, stupid. Don't repeat yourself. Max ~30 lines per method, ~300 lines per file.
- **Architecture:** Clean Architecture. Thin APIs/Controllers. No business logic in the routing layer. Nextcloud App ecosystem standards.
- **Docs:** Read `AGENTS.md` before proposing changes. Add documentation comments to EVERY public member.
- **Testing:** Every new feature needs unit tests. Every bug fix needs a regression test. Use BDD style naming.
- **Questions:** Batch questions at the end of the session with 2-3 options. Don't guess.
- **Workflow:** Always check `docs/backlog/ACTIVE_TASKS.md` before starting work. Update it when starting, during, and completing tasks. Follow Coding→Review workflow from `AGENTS.md`.
- **Review:** Fix minor issues immediately during review. Ask user for unclear issues. Move major refactors to backlog.
